.codex-worklog.md
.codex-worklog-*.md
BUG_FINDINGS.md
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
# Contents rather than the directory itself, for the reason spelled out at
# /.superpowers/ below: git never descends into an EXCLUDED directory, so a negation
# inside one can never re-include anything. Everything under diagnostics/ stays local
# EXCEPT issue106-dumps/, which the test suite reads directly -- four classes in
# tests/test_diagnostics.py decode the one real optCompatibility matrix anyone has
# captured, deliberately without a skip, so an ignored copy means a red CI on a clean
# checkout (measured: 21 failures). The capture is redacted at source by the reporter.
/diagnostics/*
!/diagnostics/issue106-dumps/
# Local working artifacts (not versioned)
/apk/
/docs/hon-internal-notes.md
/docs/superpowers/

# Local development and agent tooling
/.gitnexus/
/.claude/
# Written by `gitnexus analyze`: the same skill files it puts under .claude/skills/,
# copied for non-Claude agents. Regenerated on every analyze.
/.agents/
# Contents rather than the directory itself: git never descends into an EXCLUDED
# directory, so a negation inside one can never re-include anything. The campaign
# records under sdd/ are tracked, and the previous `/.superpowers/` ignored every new
# one silently: they landed only when someone remembered `git add -f`, and the
# committed ones stayed visible purely because a tracked file outranks .gitignore.
# The agent tooling beside sdd/ stays ignored.
# NB: some setups also carry an untracked `.superpowers/sdd/.gitignore` holding `*`,
# written by local tooling. That wins over this rule in those working copies, so
# `git add -f` may still be needed there. It is not part of this repository.
/.superpowers/*
!/.superpowers/sdd/
/AGENTS.md
/CLAUDE.md
/.development/

# Local test and analysis output
/.pytest_cache/
/.mypy_cache/
/.ruff_cache/
/.coverage
/coverage.xml
/htmlcov/
/.venv/
